WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
Speaker 1: I want to start today with some rare&nbsp;
good news when it comes to just the process of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:11.440
voting in the United States. You know, we're&nbsp;
we're waiting to see whether Democrats will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:16.400
able to push forward the voting rights bill&nbsp;
that Joe Biden has been talking about now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:23.920
intensely for the last week or so. But&nbsp;
absent that, there are so many different ways&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:30.320
in which Republicans are not even fighting the&nbsp;
so-called battle of ideas which they claim to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:39.120
prioritize, and instead fighting to win elections&nbsp;
by subterfuge and deception and systems control,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:43.840
rather than winning people's hearts and&nbsp;
minds. So gerrymandering is one of these ways&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:50.960
that Republicans have sought to and have&nbsp;
benefited from manipulating the system,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:57.120
reducing ballot boxes in minority neighborhoods,&nbsp;
limiting voting hours, trying to stop mail in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:04.560
ballots, mandating specific IDs, including IDs&nbsp;
that require that while themselves may be free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:12.080
required documents which, if you don't have&nbsp;
them, are not free to obtain putting in place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:17.760
Partizan actors to oversee the count or&nbsp;
whatever the case may be, it's relentless.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:24.000
It's exhausting. And the first element of that&nbsp;
that I mentioned is gerrymandering. And we have,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.200
you know, you've got to look at this big battle or&nbsp;
this big war and the different battles within it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:34.560
Within the battle around gerrymandering.&nbsp;
We have a little bit of good news in one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:41.200
those sub battles, and that news is that the Ohio&nbsp;
Supreme Court has decided to throw into the trash&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:49.280
the Republican gerrymandered maps and has given&nbsp;
10 days, 10 days to fix it. The AP reporting the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:55.120
Ohio Supreme Court declared Republican drawn&nbsp;
legislative maps invalid Wednesday yesterday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:00.720
agreeing with voting rights advocates that the&nbsp;
lines were unconstitutionally gerrymandered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:06.960
in a four two three ruling. The court sent the&nbsp;
maps back to the Ohio Redistricting Commission&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:14.400
to take another crack at complying with provisions&nbsp;
of a 2015 state constitutional amendment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:19.920
which requires there be an attempt at&nbsp;
avoiding Partizan favoritism. These&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:26.400
maps in Ohio are so gerrymandered that there isn't&nbsp;
even evidence that they tried to avoid Partizan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:31.120
favoritism. Justices gave the panel 10 days and&nbsp;
retained jurisdiction to review the handiwork.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.000
The dispute comes amid the process of&nbsp;
redrawing legislative and congressional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:42.240
district maps that states must undertake once a&nbsp;
decade to reflect changes from the U.S. Census.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:49.360
There's a bunch of interesting elements here,&nbsp;
one of which is Republican Gov. Mike DeWine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:57.040
a member of the commission and whose son&nbsp;
was among Wednesday's dissenting justices,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:02.960
pledged in a statement to work with my fellow&nbsp;
redistricting commission members on revised maps.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:11.600
Think about that. Republican Mike DeWine is a&nbsp;
member of the redistricting commission and his son&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:19.120
is one of the justices of the Supreme Court who&nbsp;
said the maps are fine that my dad was involved in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:26.880
in in drawing and writing. I mean, it's it's, you&nbsp;
know, there are so many ways in which this is just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:33.120
absolutely insane and you've got to fight these&nbsp;
battles one by one. And this is the difficulty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:38.000
when they have so many ways, you know, they&nbsp;
talk about winning the battle of ideas.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:43.840
And the problem is they've lost the battle of&nbsp;
ideas. When you look at the country and you say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:49.680
do most people believe that the government&nbsp;
has a basic duty to provide some health care&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:53.920
to everybody, regardless of ability to pay?&nbsp;
Very popular statement not reflected in our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:58.880
elected officials, not reflected in the actions&nbsp;
of our elected officials. When you say, well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:04.080
what's the position on abortion nationally?&nbsp;
Well, legal in most cases is the opinion of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.800
more people than ever before in the United States.&nbsp;
Is that reflected in our elected officials? No.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:14.240
They're not winning people over in&nbsp;
terms of hearts and minds in policy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:19.680
They're winning with gerrymandering, making voting&nbsp;
difficult for the people that they think would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:24.320
to their advantage to make voting difficult for&nbsp;
all of the other things that I mentioned. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:30.240
then when you even take the war and then you look&nbsp;
at one battle gerrymandering and you look at that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:36.640
battle in one state, Ohio, you find, oh, one of&nbsp;
the guys who was involved in drawing these lines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:43.600
which are crazy Partizan was Mike DeWine. And&nbsp;
one of the justices on the Ohio Supreme Court&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:50.240
deciding as to whether those lines are OK or&nbsp;
not is the son of Mike DeWine. It's just it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:54.880
truly stunning that this is what's going on&nbsp;
in this country, but it is. And so we've got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.880 --> 00:05:00.400
to fight these battles one by one, the battle.&nbsp;
It's not even that it's been won yet. In Ohio,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:06.160
there's the opportunity to win it by getting more&nbsp;
